  "termDescription": "Inflation is a sustained rise in the general price level, reported as the percentage change in a price index against the same month a year earlier. In the United States it is measured two ways: the Consumer Price Index from the Bureau of Labor Statistics, and the personal consumption expenditures price index from the Bureau of Economic Analysis.",
