  "termDescription": "Support and resistance are price areas where buying or selling interest has repeatedly halted a move. Support is the area below the current price where declines have found a floor. Resistance is the area above where advances have stalled. The concept is set out in Edwards and Magee, Technical Analysis of Stock Trends, chapter 13. It is not defined or standardized by any regulator.",
