  "metaDesc": "A charge-off is an accounting entry on the creditor's books, not a released debt. The two clocks that actually matter, and what paying or settling changes.",
  "ogTitle": "Charge-Off &mdash; Learn the Lingo",
  "ogDesc": "A charge-off doesn't mean the debt is gone &mdash; it means the lender moved it to the loss column. Here's which clock is running, what a collector can do, and what a paid charge-off actually changes.",
