   "<li>Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System, <a href=\"https://www.federalreserve.gov/publications/files/scf23.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Changes in U.S. Family Finances from 2019 to 2022: Evidence from the Survey of Consumer Finances</a> &mdash; the definition quoted on this page, the 2022 median of $192,900 and mean of $1,063,700, the medians and means by age, and the bottom-quartile figures of &minus;$5,300 (2022) and &minus;$15,700 (2019). All in 2022 dollars.</li>",
