   "<li>Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System, <a href=\"https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/pressreleases/other20250228a.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Federal Reserve Board begins 2025 Survey of Consumer Finances</a>, 28 February 2025 &mdash; the 2025 field period and the statement that summary results will be published in late 2026.</li>",
   "<li>Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System, <a href=\"https://www.federalreserve.gov/econres/scf/dataviz/scf/table/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Survey of Consumer Finances interactive tables, 1989&ndash;2022</a> &mdash; the historical series behind the age brackets, for readers who want other cuts of the same data.</li>",
   "<li>Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System, <a href=\"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/z1/dataviz/dfa/distribute/table/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Distributional Financial Accounts: Distribution of Household Wealth in the U.S.</a> &mdash; the Fed's quarterly aggregate wealth distribution, updated far more often than the triennial SCF and the place to look between waves.</li>",
   "<li>Internal Revenue Service, <a href=\"https://www.irs.gov/taxtopics/tc558\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Topic no. 558, Additional tax on early distributions from retirement plans other than IRAs</a> &mdash; the 10% additional tax on the portion includible in gross income for distributions before age 59&frac12;, and the list of exceptions.</li>",
   "<li>Internal Revenue Service, <a href=\"https://www.irs.gov/publications/p575\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Publication 575, Pension and Annuity Income</a> &mdash; that distributions of pre-tax retirement contributions and their earnings are included in gross income when withdrawn, which is the tax embedded in a traditional 401(k) balance.</li>",
   "<li>U.S. Census Bureau, <a href=\"https://www.census.gov/library/publications/2025/demo/p70br-211.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wealth of Households: 2023</a> &mdash; a second federal wealth series, built from the Survey of Income and Program Participation, cited here only to establish that it exists, uses different definitions and is not interchangeable with the SCF.</li>"
