  "title": "Sinking Fund: What It Is and How to Set One Up | Learn the Lingo",
  "metaDesc": "A sinking fund is money set aside monthly for a bill you already know is coming. The arithmetic, a six-fund table, and where an emergency fund takes over.",
  "ogTitle": "Sinking Fund &mdash; Learn the Lingo",
  "ogDesc": "The registration renewal is not an emergency. It is on the calendar. A sinking fund is what turns a $175 March bill into a $25 line your budget can actually see.",
