  "termDescription": "Supplemental Security Income (SSI) is a monthly cash payment from the federal government to people who are aged 65 or older, blind, or disabled and who also have very little income and almost no countable assets. It is authorized by Title XVI of the Social Security Act, 42 U.S.C. section 1381 and following, with operating rules at 20 CFR part 416, and it is paid from general revenue rather than the Social Security trust funds. SSI is needs-based and is not the same program as Social Security Disability Insurance, which is an insurance benefit earned through payroll-tax work credits.",
