  "termDescription": "Bollinger Bands are three lines plotted over a price chart: a moving average, normally 20 periods, with an upper and a lower band placed a set number of standard deviations away from that average, normally two, measured on the same window of closing prices. John Bollinger developed them in the 1980s. The bands widen when recent price movement has been volatile and narrow when it has been quiet.",
