  "termDescription": "A breakout is price moving decisively out of a trading range, or through a support or resistance level it had previously respected. No exchange, regulator or standards body defines how far past the level price must move, on what timeframe, or whether the move is measured on a closing price or an intraday touch, so whether a breakout happened is a judgment call rather than a fact. Traders add confirmation rules such as a closing break, expanding volume, a successful retest or a percentage buffer, and all of those are conventions of practice with no published authority behind them.",
