   "<b>The two most serious tests of the theory disagree.</b> Alfred Cowles (<i>Econometrica</i>, 1933) found Hamilton's forecasts returned <b>12% a year against 15.5%</b> for simply staying invested. Brown, Goetzmann and Kumar (<i>Journal of Finance</i>, 1998) re-ran the same record and found <b>positive risk-adjusted alpha of roughly 290 basis points</b>. Neither is a hit rate for the confirmation rule, and no page should print one.",
