   "<li>Alfred Cowles 3rd, <a href=\"https://cowles.yale.edu/sites/default/files/2022-08/cowles-forecasters33.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">&ldquo;Can Stock Market Forecasters Forecast?&rdquo;, <i>Econometrica</i> vol. 1, no. 3 (1933), pp. 309&ndash;324</a>, hosted by the Cowles Foundation at Yale &mdash; 255 forecasting editorials from December 1903 to December 1929, 12% vs 15.5% on the industrials, 5.7% vs 7.7% on the railroads, 45 of 90 position changes successful, and the quoted conclusion.</li>",
