   "<b>MACD is built from averages of past closes, so it cannot lead price.</b> It is a lagging indicator wearing momentum&rsquo;s clothing, and Aspray &mdash; who built the histogram &mdash; wrote that its &ldquo;signals often lag.&rdquo;",
   "<b>MACD is unbounded and denominated in the stock&rsquo;s own dollars,</b> so a reading of +4.00 on one stock and +0.08 on another can describe an identical move. Unlike <a href=\"relative-strength-index-rsi.html\">RSI</a>, it is not comparable across stocks or across time."
