   "<li>Clifford S. Asness, Andrea Frazzini, Ronen Israel, Tobias J. Moskowitz and Lasse Heje Pedersen, <a href=\"https://econpapers.repec.org/RePEc:eee:jfinec:v:129:y:2018:i:3:p:479-509\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">&ldquo;Size matters, if you control your junk&rdquo;</a>, <em>Journal of Financial Economics</em> 129(3), 2018, pp. 479&ndash;509 &mdash; source for the list of standing objections to the size premium quoted on this page. Earlier literature referenced: Rolf W. Banz, &ldquo;The relationship between return and market value of common stocks,&rdquo; <em>Journal of Financial Economics</em> 9(1), 1981, pp. 3&ndash;18; and Joel Horowitz, Tim Loughran and N. E. Savin, &ldquo;Three analyses of the firm size premium,&rdquo; <em>Journal of Empirical Finance</em> 7(2), 2000, pp. 143&ndash;153.</li>"
