  "termDescription": "A moving average is the average price of a security over a fixed number of the most recent periods, recalculated each period so that the oldest value drops out as the newest one is added. A simple moving average (SMA) weights every period in the window equally; an exponential moving average (EMA) weights recent periods more heavily using a smoothing constant of 2 divided by the period count plus one. Because every value in it is a past price, a moving average is a lagging indicator by construction.",
