  "h1": "Dividend Yield",
  "heroSub": "Annual dividends per share divided by the current share price &mdash; which means the number goes <em>up</em> when the stock goes down. That one piece of arithmetic explains most of the trouble people get into with it.",
  "aka": "the yield &middot; current yield &middot; indicated yield &middot; trailing yield &middot; forward yield",
