  "termDescription": "An index fund is a pooled investment fund whose stated objective is to track the return of a specified market index rather than to outperform it. Because the manager follows a published rulebook instead of researching and selecting securities, the fund needs no research staff and trades less, which is where its lower cost comes from. The SEC describes an index fund as following a passive investment strategy designed to achieve approximately the same return as a particular index before fees.",
