   "<li>William F. Sharpe, <a href=\"https://web.stanford.edu/~wfsharpe/art/active/active.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">&ldquo;The Arithmetic of Active Management&rdquo;</a>, <em>The Financial Analysts' Journal</em>, Vol. 47, No. 1, January/February 1991, pp. 7 to 9 (the definitions of passive and active investors, and the two conclusions that before costs the average actively managed dollar equals the average passively managed dollar and after costs earns less).</li>",
