   "<li>Economic Report of the President, 2010, <a href=\"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/ERP-2010/html/ERP-2010-other-3.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Chapter 2: Rescuing the Economy from the Great Recession</a> (the S&amp;P 500 declining 29 percent in the second half of 2008, standing 65 percent above its March low at the end of 2009, and household and nonprofit net worth falling 20 percent, or about $13 trillion, between December 2007 and December 2008).</li>",
   "<li>Legal Information Institute, <a href=\"https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/15/80a-5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">15 U.S.C. &sect; 80a-5</a> (the definition of a &ldquo;diversified company&rdquo; at subsection (b)(1) &mdash; at least 75 per centum of total assets with no single issuer above 5 per centum of total assets and no more than 10 per centum of an issuer's voting securities &mdash; and &ldquo;non-diversified company&rdquo; at (b)(2)).</li>",
   "<li>U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission, <a href=\"https://www.sec.gov/investment/divisionsinvestmentsecurities-lending-open-closed-end-investment-companieshtm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Securities Lending by U.S. Open-End and Closed-End Investment Companies</a> (collateral at least equal to the value of the borrowed securities and marked to market daily, and lending income from borrower fees and/or reinvestment of cash collateral), and SEC Office of Investor Education and Advocacy, <a href=\"https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/general-resources/news-alerts/alerts-bulletins/investor-bulletins/fractional-share-investing-buying-slice-instead-whole-share\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Investor Bulletin: Fractional Share Investing</a> (availability varying by firm, fractional shares generally not transferable to another brokerage firm, and liquidity not guaranteed).</li>"
