  "termDescription": "A recession is a significant decline in economic activity that is spread across the economy and lasts more than a few months. In the United States it is dated by the Business Cycle Dating Committee of the National Bureau of Economic Research, a private nonprofit, which judges depth, diffusion and duration across a set of monthly indicators. The committee explicitly does not use the widely repeated rule of two consecutive quarters of falling real GDP, and it names peaks and troughs retrospectively, sometimes more than a year after they occur.",
