  "metaDesc": "What debt-to-income ratio means, what counts in it, and why the 43% mortgage limit was replaced in 2022 &mdash; with a worked example in real dollars.",
  "ogTitle": "Debt-to-Income Ratio &mdash; Learn the Lingo",
  "ogDesc": "Almost every article online still says 43 percent is the legal DTI ceiling for a mortgage. The CFPB deleted that number, and the rule that replaced it does not mention DTI at all. Here is what actually applies, with the arithmetic done in dollars.",
  "eyebrow": "Credit &amp; Borrowing",
