  "termDescription": "A deductible is the fixed dollar amount an insured person must pay toward covered services in a plan year before the insurer begins paying its share. After the deductible is met the insured normally still owes coinsurance or copays until reaching the plan&rsquo;s out-of-pocket maximum.",
