   "<b>A high-deductible health plan is a defined thing, not a description.</b> For 2026 it means a deductible of at least <b>$1,700 self-only / $3,400 family</b> and an out-of-pocket maximum no higher than <b>$8,500 / $17,000</b>. Only a plan meeting that definition makes you eligible to contribute to an HSA.",
